I think that everything that we live  with has a clear purpose and everything  and design is a virus for me so it sort  of infects everything that you do in a  positive way my name is Josh Owen I'm  chair of the industrial design program  and an associate at the Vignelli Center  for design studies here at RIT I've  always felt that products should speak  for themselves and I know there's irony  and the fact that I'm you know I behave  as a designer author yet I prefer to see  objects you know speak for themselves I  don't think that they need to be dressed  up by a designer name or by a brand I  don't feel that that my authorship  should change the way people perceive of  the object whether that's the espresso  machine or one of my objects I think  they should all speak clearly and  honestly from their formal attributes  without the need of brand identity a  good object can be like a paperclip you  know just kind of perfect and it's an  inception and almost invisible in the  landscape of things at the same time  that paperclip is a unbelievable story  of heroics and manufacturing and  technology and that's the way I'd like  to see many of my objects was fitting  into that kind of a context I test the  things that I design by living with them  by using them by experiencing them by  passing them along that is all very  important to me in in the role that I  play as an educator as a human being  many of the objects in the house or  objects I designed everything that we  live with has a story from the hardware  to the software to the  the structure every element here is its  own book it's very real to me and those  stories are very important to tell to my  children to tell to others to experience  to drink in the richness of life people  have come into the spaces that my wife  and I have lived in and said there's no  art on the walls and we say but the  walls are art you know the objects are  art everything's got a story I do aspire  to make things which have an iconic  sensibility so that maybe when people  make decisions about them they're  thinking this is something that all I'll  pass along with something which  functionally speaking won't go bad
 

